e in the second house and april must be in the third house.", "S13: mar == 2.", "S14: april == 3.", "S15: march == 2.", "Clue 1 tells us arnold is in the first house, so arnold must be in the first house and bob must be in the second house.", "S16: arnold == 1.",", "Clue 2 tells us there is one house between carol and alice, so carol must be in the fourth house and alice must be in the third house.", "S17: carol == 4.", "S18: alice == 3.", "S19: bob == 1.", "S20: arnold == 1.", "S21: bob == 2.",", "S22: alice == 3.",", "S23: carol == 4.",",", "S24: And(bob == 1, bob!= 5, jan == 3, Eric == 3, feb == 5, may == 6, mar == 2, april == 3, sept == 4, arnold == 1, alice == 3, carol == 4).", "solution": {"header": ["House", "Name", "Birthday"], "rows": [["1", "Arnold", "sept"], ["2", "Bob", "jan"], ["3", "Alice", "april"], ["4", "Carol", "may"], ["5", "Eric", "feb"], ["6", "Peter", "mar"]]}}
