ll == 3.", "Clue 5 confirms Peter is not in the sixth house, and since Carol is in house 1, Peter must be in house 1.", "S11: Peter == 1.", "Clue 1 tells us Carol is not in the sixth house, and since Peter is in house 1, Carol must be in house 1.", "S12: Carol == 1.", "Clue 2 confirms there is one house between Bob and the very tall person, and since the very tall person is in house 5, Bob must be in house 3.", "S13: Bob == 3.", "Clue 9 confirms the short person is not in the third house, but since the short person is in house 4, the short person must be the person between Bob and the very tall person.", "S14: short == 4.", "Clue 10 confirms the very short person is to the right of the very tall person, and since the very tall person is in house 5, the very short person must be in house 6.", "S15: very_short == 6.", "Clue 11 confirms Carol is not in the second house, but since Carol is in house 1, the only possibility is that Carol is the average person.", "S16: average == 2.", "Clue 5 confirms Peter is not in the sixth house, but since Peter is in house 1, Arnold must be in house 6.", "S17: Arnold == 6.", "Clue 1 confirms Carol is not in the sixth house, but since Arnold is in house 6, Carol must be in house 1.", "S18: Carol == 1.", "With all clues satisfied, the solution is clear."], "solution": {"header": ["House", "Name", "Height"], "rows": [["1", "Peter", "average"], ["2", "Carol", "short"], ["3", "Bob", "tall"], ["4", "Arnold", "very_short"], ["5", "Eric", "very_tall"], ["6", "Alice", "super_tall"]]}}
